From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:28:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Add the speaker amps' shutdown
 line

The six speaker amps of the MacBook Pro 14" M4 (J604) share one
shutdown line (SDZ): AP GPIO 15, the function-reset of the ADT's
/arm-io/i2c3/audio-speaker, with the same flags as on the J713. Describe
it as a fixed regulator, as the J616s and J713 do, so that the amps can
take it as their SDZ supply and one amp's fault can drop it for all six.

Nothing uses it yet; an unused fixed regulator is switched off at late
init, which keeps the amps in hardware shutdown.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 108f5ea7b6..848a5530a5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -60,6 +60,20 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The speaker amps' shared shutdown line (SDZ, AP GPIO 15, the ADT
+	 * function-reset of /arm-io/i2c3/audio-speaker; low = shutdown). One
+	 * fixed regulator, the SDZ supply of all six amps, as on the J616s and
+	 * J713: one amp's fault takes the whole group down. Without a consumer
+	 * it is switched off at late init, which holds the amps in shutdown.
+	 */
+	speaker_sdz: regulator-sn012776-sdz {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "sn012776-sdz";
+		gpios = <&pinctrl_ap 15 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>; /* DTV-SPK-3 */
+		enable-active-high;
+	};
+
 	/*
 	 * The headphone jack: the AOP audio component's jack back-end (DAI 4)
 	 * to the CS42L84, as a card of its own.
